    "narrative": "Heading into today\u2019s slate, **Kyle Tucker** remains our cornerstone, topping the board with a 66.04 efficiency score despite the lack of a confirmed starter, anchoring an offense that is leaning heavily on favorable platoon splits. **Jackson Merrill** (51.88) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (50.68) serve as the most tactical plays today; both benefit significantly from a positive dynamic platoon adjustment against right-handed pitching, which helps neutralize the skill of Rasmussen and Misiorowski. **Luis Lara** (54.02) is our most aggressive start, as his high floor is bolstered by a favorable 4.98 xERA matchup against Robbie Ray, providing the optimal environment to chase stolen bases and volume without sacrificing too much batting average.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Brayan Rocchio**, who narrowly missed the cut with a 36.43 score. While his profile typically provides the speed we covet, the optimizer penalized his projected #9 spot in the order and the matchup against an efficient arm like Smith, pushing him below our strict 40.0 \"Zebras\" floor. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Drake Baldwin** and **Liam Hicks**, both of whom carry high-risk profiles today; **Drake Baldwin** faces an elite 2.85 xERA arm in Skubal, and **Liam Hicks** is contending with a similarly difficult matchup against Cole. We are monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for these starters closely; any shifts in batting order\u2014specifically if **Andy Pages** is moved down from his assumed #7 slot\u2014could further compress our offensive ceiling today.",
